# This repository is consumed as a *named build context* by the applications built on it:
#
#   docker build --build-context form-builder=../form-builder …
#
# and a named context has no .dockerignore of its own to fall back on — the application's
# .dockerignore applies only to the application's own context. Without this file, a developer's
# `target/` (a full compiled tree, plus whatever JDK compiled it) and `node_modules/` are
# transferred into every image build that names this directory.
#
# Stage 1 of those builds runs `sbt publishLocal` here, so everything it needs is the source,
# build.sbt and project/*.sbt — all of which are kept.
**/target
**/node_modules
.git
.bsp
.bloop
.metals
.scala-build
